# The shared-actions repo, declared here as an ordinary sibling because
# `tests/e2e/codetracer-subset/t_e2e_codetracer_in_place_project_file.nim`
# READS A FILE OUT OF IT: `reprobuild-provision/provision-reprobuild-siblings.sh`
# is the oracle for the CodeTracer Nim-gitlink provisioning contract, and
# `repro_test_support.requireMetacraftGithubActionsRoot` raises rather than
# skipping when the checkout is absent — per the suite's no-silent-skip rule,
# a missing prerequisite fails loudly and names itself.
#
# `uses: metacraft-labs/metacraft-github-actions/...@dev` does NOT satisfy that
# read. GitHub materialises a composite action under the runner's private
# `_actions/` tree, not adjacent to the checkout, so a job that references ten
# of these actions still has no sibling directory for the test to open.
#
# Until now the only thing that produced one was a bespoke `clone-repo` step in
# `ci.yml`, which covered exactly the one job that step was written into and
# nothing else — no other CI job, and no developer workspace. That is the gap
# these three cases reported: a workspace built from reprobuild's project set
# alone never gets this repo, and the cases fail on every local run. Declaring
# it here puts the prerequisite in the blessed clone-list that
# `docs/repository-requirements.md` designates for exactly this purpose,
# as data rather than as one workflow's inline step.
metacraft-github-actions=dev

